# Credentials for `pnpm event:sync` (OpenMeet).
#
# This file is gitignored. Never commit real credentials.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Use a dedicated bot account, not your personal login.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Create one through the normal sign-up form:
#
#     https://platform.openmeet.net
#
# OpenMeet's own guidance — "Programmatic / automation access" in the API auth
# docs — says to use a dedicated bot account rather than a real person's login:
#
#   https://github.com/OpenMeet-Team/openmeet-api/blob/main/docs/auth.md#programmatic--automation-access
#
# Why it matters, since nothing enforces it:
#
#   * A bot account can be revoked or have its password rotated without
#     disrupting anyone's browser session.
#   * The sync acts as the account that owns it. You do not want a script
#     running unattended under your own identity, where a mistake or a
#     compromise hits your account rather than a throwaway one.
#
# There is nothing special about a bot account: it is an ordinary account with
# an ordinary email and password. No API key, personal access token or service
# account type exists to set — automation just logs in as a user and then
# refreshes the returned token.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# If you signed up with an AT Protocol handle (Bluesky) and have no password
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# You can set one: PATCH /api/v1/auth/me with `{"password": "..."}` is accepted
# for passwordless accounts without requiring the current password. But think
# twice — that puts a password on your *personal* account, which is exactly what
# the bot account above exists to avoid. Prefer a separate account.
#
# The alternative is ATProto service auth, which needs a Bluesky *app password*
# instead of an OpenMeet one and is documented in the link above. The tooling
# does not implement that path yet.

OPENMEET_EMAIL=bot-account@example.com
OPENMEET_PASSWORD=